# UC-012 · Search

> Partial of `docs/use-cases/UC-012-search-orders/`. Owner: `search-architect`.
> Inherits the engine and the freshness tolerance from `00-use-case.md` and the port from
> `10-domain.md` — doesn't redecide them. Contains no code; the mapping file is the one block
> written in full. Form references in `.claude/skills/search-architect/templates/`.
> Rules applied, never reproduced: `@.claude/rules/search.md`.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Mother spec | `00-use-case.md` |
| Kind of case | read — `Trigger`: inbound REST adapter |
| Why this partial exists | `00-use-case.md` § Search index: "Order → Elasticsearch projection" |
| Source of truth | `Order`, `Storage`: relational (UC-003, `20-persistence.md`) |
| Search package | `adapter.out.search` (blueprint `packages.map`) |
| Divergences from other partials | none |

## 1 · Projection

First case of the `orders` projection: this block fixes it, and later cases inherit it.

| Source field | Search field | Type | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| `Order.id` | `id` (document id) and `orderId` | `keyword` | the unique sort tiebreaker; returned |
| `Order.number` | `orderNumber` | `keyword` | exact filter; returned |
| `Customer.name` (carried by the event) | `customerName` | `text` + `keyword` sub-field | searched by words; returned |
| `Order.status` | `status` | `keyword` | filter |
| `Order.total` | `totalMinor` | `long` (minor units) | range filter |
| `Order.placedAt` | `placedAt` | `date`, `date_time` | sort; returned |
| `Order.lines[].sku`, `.quantity` | `lines` | `nested` (`sku` `keyword`, `quantity` `integer`) | "contains SKU X" filter |
| — | `deleted` | `boolean` | tombstone filter |

Not projected: shipping address, payment data — nothing searches or shows them
(`@.claude/rules/personal-data.md`).

## 2 · Index

| Fact | Value |
|---|---|
| Alias | `orders` |
| Version | 1 → index `orders-v1` |
| Primary shards | 1 |
| Replicas | `app.search.replicas`: 0 local and test, 1 in production |
| Refresh interval | `1s` |

`src/main/resources/search/orders-v1.json`:

```json
{
  "settings": { "number_of_shards": 1, "refresh_interval": "1s" },
  "mappings": {
    "dynamic": "strict",
    "properties": {
      "orderId": { "type": "keyword" },
      "orderNumber": { "type": "keyword" },
      "customerName": { "type": "text", "fields": { "keyword": { "type": "keyword", "ignore_above": 256 } } },
      "status": { "type": "keyword" },
      "totalMinor": { "type": "long" },
      "placedAt": { "type": "date", "format": "date_time" },
      "lines": { "type": "nested", "properties": { "sku": { "type": "keyword" }, "quantity": { "type": "integer" } } },
      "deleted": { "type": "boolean" }
    }
  }
}
```

## 3 · Queries

| Port method | Match | Filters | Sort | Page | Returns |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `SearchOrdersPort.search(query, after, size)` | `customerName` (`match`, the reader's words) | `deleted = false`; `status` when given | `placedAt` desc, `orderId` desc | ceiling 100; cursor = the last hit's sort values | `OrderSearchPage.Item(orderId, orderNumber, customerName, status, placedAt)` — never the aggregate |

A reader who acts on an order loads it through `LoadOrderPort` — the search result is a copy.

## 4 · Writes

none — the read case. The indexer is UC-013-index-order.

## 5 · Rebuild

none — the rebuild is UC-014-rebuild-orders-index.

## 6 · Lag

| Part | Duration |
|---|---|
| Outbox poll (`35-jobs.md` of UC-003) | up to 1 s |
| Consumer (UC-013) | under 1 s at the expected rate |
| Refresh interval | 1 s |
| **Lag consumed** | **3 s** |
| `Freshness` of this case | 10 s — "a new order may take a few seconds to appear in the search" |
| Remainder for a cache over `SearchOrdersPort` | 7 s |

## 7 · Failure

| Port method | Engine unreachable or alias missing | The read |
|---|---|---|
| `search` | `DependencyUnavailableException` (`ORDER_SEARCH_UNAVAILABLE`) | fails — `00-use-case.md` § Errors: "search temporarily unavailable"; no fallback to the database |

## 8 · Requirements to other partials

| Partial | Requirement |
|---|---|
| `10-domain.md` | Port `SearchOrdersPort`, kind `search index`, returning `OrderSearchPage`; event `OrderChanged` carrying the order snapshot and the source version (UC-013 consumes it) |
| `20-persistence.md` (UC-003) | `Order` keeps a version that grows on every write, and `OrderChanged` is appended to the outbox in the same transaction |
| `22-cache.md` | none in this case; a cache would be bounded by § 6's remainder |

## 9 · Declared dependencies

| Dependency | Version | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-starter-data-elasticsearch` | (managed by the Boot parent) | `ElasticsearchOperations`, the Elasticsearch client |

## 10 · Configuration

| Property | Value | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `spring.elasticsearch.uris` | `${SEARCH_URIS:http://localhost:${SEARCH_PORT:9200}}` | local runs over HTTP; production sets HTTPS and the bundle |
| `spring.elasticsearch.username` / `password` | `${SEARCH_USERNAME:elastic}` / `${SEARCH_PASSWORD}` — no default | `@.claude/rules/secrets.md` |
| `spring.elasticsearch.connection-timeout` / `socket-timeout` | `2s` / `5s` | a search slower than 5 s is a failure for this screen |
| `app.search.replicas` | `0` local, `1` production | § 2 |

Full shape in `templates/application-search.yml.example`.

